<#
.SYNOPSIS
    This PowerShell script renames the built-in Guest account to a non-default name
    to satisfy the requirement that the Guest account must not be named "Guest".
.NOTES
    Author          : Terrance Fortson
    LinkedIn        : linkedin.com/in/terrancefortson/
    GitHub          : github.com/terrcyber
    Date Created    : 2026-03-12
    Last Modified   : 2026-03-12
    Version         : 1.0
    CVEs            : N/A
    Plugin IDs      : N/A
    STIG-ID         : WN11-SO-000025
.TESTED ON
    Date(s) Tested  : 
    Tested By       : 
    Systems Tested  : 
    PowerShell Ver. : 
.USAGE
    Run with administrative privileges.
    Example syntax:
    PS C:\> .\WN11-SO-000025_remediation.ps1
#>

Rename-LocalUser -Name "Guest" -NewName "Onboard"

Write-Host "STIG WN11-SO-000025 remediation applied successfully." -ForegroundColor Green
